---
title: thoughts on minimalism
---
date: 2024-01-10
---
excerpt: why less is often more, especially in software design and daily life.
---
body:

Minimalism isn't about austerity—it's about clarity. Whether I'm pruning a machine learning pipeline or tidying a
living space, I keep rediscovering how removing friction reveals the work that matters. In this piece I explore a few
rituals that help keep projects focused and ensure the teams around me can think clearly about what comes next.
